1
00:00:00,269 --> 00:00:01,617
(Q1) Thorndyke's.

2
00:00:01,617 --> 00:00:04,397
Good morning. Is that Mr Thorndyke?

3
00:00:04,397 --> 00:00:06,504
Speaking. How can I help?

4
00:00:06,504 --> 00:00:13,849
I've got quite a few things which need painting and fixing in the flat and I wonder whether you'd be able to do the work.

5
00:00:13,849 --> 00:00:17,674
I'm sure I'd be able to help but let me take down a few details.

6
00:00:17,674 --> 00:00:19,419
Yes, of course.

7
00:00:19,419 --> 00:00:22,632
Well, firstly, how did you hear about us?

8
00:00:22,632 --> 00:00:29,648
(Qexample) It was my friend May Hampton ... you did some excellent work for her a couple of years ago. Do you remember?

9
00:00:29,648 --> 00:00:33,965
Oh, yes, that was in West Park Flats, lovely lady.

10
00:00:33,965 --> 00:00:35,146
Yes, she is.

11
00:00:35,146 --> 00:00:37,527
And what's your name, please?

12
00:00:37,527 --> 00:00:39,513
It's Edith Pargetter.

13
00:00:39,513 --> 00:00:43,369
Edith ... can you spell your surname, please? Edith……

14
00:00:43,369 --> 00:00:49,425
[Q1答案句] It's P-A-R-G-E-double T-E-R.

15
00:00:49,425 --> 00:00:51,178
Double T, right.&nbsp;

16
00:00:51,178 --> 00:00:53,822
(Q2) And do you live in West Park Flats as well?

17
00:00:53,822 --> 00:00:58,407
[Q2答案句] No, actually it's East Park, Flat 4.

18
00:00:58,407 --> 00:01:03,128
(Q3) Oh, right, that's over the road, I seem to remember - quite difficult to get to.

19
00:01:03,128 --> 00:01:06,097
[Q3答案句] Yes. it's at the back of the library.

20
00:01:06,097 --> 00:01:09,768
(Q4) Right, I know. And what's your phone number?

21
00:01:09,768 --> 00:01:17,500
875934 but I'm out a great deal in the afternoons and evenings.&nbsp;

22
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:20,692
[Q4答案句] So would the best time to ring you be in the morning?

23
00:01:20,692 --> 00:01:21,659
[Q4答案句-确认] Yes.

24
00:01:21,659 --> 00:01:29,723
(Q5) Fine. I've made a note of that. Can I just ask, I'll be in a van and I know parking's rather difficult round your flats.

25
00:01:29,723 --> 00:01:31,405
Where would you recommend?

26
00:01:31,405 --> 00:01:39,316
[Q5答案句] Well. I always tell people in larger vehicles to park by the postbox on the other side of the road from the entrance.

27
00:01:39,316 --> 00:01:41,363
Good, thanks.

28
00:01:41,363 --> 00:01:45,143
(Q6) And will you be able to give me a full itemised quote?

29
00:01:45,143 --> 00:01:49,567
[Q6答案句] Oh. Yes, I'll list all the jobs separately with individual prices.

30
00:01:49,567 --> 00:01:51,091
That'd be a great help.

31
00:01:51,091 --> 00:01:52,520
No problem.

32
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:55,029
(Q7（table横纵表格填空）) Now, what would you like me to do?

33
00:01:55,029 --> 00:01:59,798
Firstly and most urgently is in the kitchen.

34
00:01:59,798 --> 00:02:05,407
With all the weather damage, the glass in the door has cracked and I'd need that fixing ...

35
00:02:05,407 --> 00:02:07,699
I presume you mean replacing?

36
00:02:07,699 --> 00:02:10,903
Oh, yes. And as soon as possible ...

37
00:02:10,903 --> 00:02:14,140
What I'll do is come round tomorrow morning and do that immediately.

38
00:02:14,140 --> 00:02:18,483
Thank you so much. The other things aren't so urgent but...

39
00:02:18,483 --> 00:02:22,068
Now, I'll make a note of everything you want doing.

40
00:02:22,068 --> 00:02:26,250
Well, in the kitchen I'd like some painting doing.

41
00:02:26,250 --> 00:02:27,828
All the kitchen walls?

42
00:02:27,828 --> 00:02:32,038
Just the area over the cooker. It's very greasy ...

43
00:02:32,038 --> 00:02:34,477
Right ...it does tend to get that way!

44
00:02:34,477 --> 00:02:35,944
Yes!

45
00:02:35,944 --> 00:02:42,887
Well, if you want a proper job done what I'd need to do is strip the old paint and plaster it about a week before I paint it.

46
00:02:42,887 --> 00:02:48,242
Of course. Now, May tells me you also do work in the garden.

47
00:02:48,242 --> 00:02:49,234
That's right.

48
00:02:49,234 --> 00:02:52,244
Well. I'd like you to replace a fence.

49
00:02:52,244 --> 00:02:53,730
Just one?

50
00:02:53,730 --> 00:02:55,692
Yes, at the far end.

51
00:02:55,692 --> 00:02:57,476
Fine. Shouldn't be a problem.

52
00:02:57,476 --> 00:02:59,241
And that's the lot.

53
00:02:59,241 --> 00:03:04,279
Fine. Yeah, as I say I can come round tomorrow morning to look over things with you.

54
00:03:04,279 --> 00:03:05,741
That's great, thank you.

55
00:03:05,741 --> 00:03:08,241
So, I'll look forward to seeing you tomorrow at...

